    "q-342547": {
      "dom_id": "step-q342547",
      "name": "Question 2",
      "problem": "Find the Laplace transform $Y(s)=L\\{y(t)\\}$ if \n\n$$\n{y}^{′}+4y={u}_{\\pi /2}(t)\\cdot sin\\,(3t-\\frac{3\\pi }{2})\\,,\\,y(0)=-2,\n$$\n\nwhere ${u}_{\\pi /2}(t)=u\\,(t-\\frac{\\pi }{2})$ is the unit step function.\n\nYou may make use of the following result:\n\n$$\nL\\{\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\omega t\\}=\\frac{\\omega }{{s}^{2}+{\\omega }^{2}},\\,s>0\n$$\n\n$Y(s)=-\\frac{2}{s+4}\\,+\\,$\n{{field-1}},$\\,s>0$",
      "worked_solution": "First, we take the Laplace transform of both sides and use the addition and scalar multiplication properties of the Laplace transform:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}L\\{{y}^{′}+4y\\} & =L\\{{u}_{\\pi /2}(t)\\cdot sin\\,(3t-\\frac{3\\pi }{2})\\} \\\\ L\\{{y}^{′}\\}+4L\\{y\\} & =L\\{{u}_{\\pi /2}(t)\\cdot sin\\,(3t-\\frac{3\\pi }{2})\\}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTo calculate $L\\{{y}^{′}\\},$ we use the formula for the Laplace transform of a derivative and the initial condition $y(0)=-2:$\n\n$$\nL\\{{y}^{′}\\}=sY(s)-y(0)=sY(s)-(-2)=sY(s)+2\n$$\n\nTo find the transform of the right-hand side, we note that the term \n\n$$\n{u}_{\\pi /2}(t)\\cdot sin\\,(3t-\\frac{3\\pi }{2})\n$$\n\nis in the form $u(t-a)\\cdot f(t)$ where $a=\\frac{\\pi }{2}$ and $f(t)=sin\\,(3t-\\frac{3\\pi }{2}).$ This can be interpreted as time-delayed sinusoidal forcing. \n\nNow, recall that the second shifting theorem (time-shifting property) states\n\n$$\nL\\{u(t-a)\\cdot f(t)\\}={e}^{-as}\\cdot L\\{f(t+a)\\}.\n$$\n\n  \n\nSo, by the second shifting theorem, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}L\\{u\\,(t-\\frac{\\pi }{2})\\cdot sin\\,(3t-\\frac{3\\pi }{2})\\} & ={e}^{-(\\pi /2)s}\\cdot L\\{sin\\,(3\\,(t+\\frac{\\pi }{2})-\\frac{3\\pi }{2})\\} \\\\  & ={e}^{-(\\pi /2)s}\\cdot L\\{\\operatorname{sin}⁡(3t)\\} \\\\  & ={e}^{-(\\pi /2)s}\\cdot \\frac{3}{{s}^{2}+9} \\\\  & =\\frac{3{e}^{-\\pi s/2}}{{s}^{2}+9}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we substitute these back into our transformed differential equation:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}L\\{{y}^{′}\\}+4L\\{y\\} & =L\\{{u}_{\\pi /2}(t)sin\\,(3t-\\frac{3\\pi }{2})\\} \\\\ (sY(s)+2)+4Y(s) & =\\frac{3{e}^{-\\pi s/2}}{{s}^{2}+9} \\\\ (s+4)Y(s)+2 & =\\frac{3{e}^{-\\pi s/2}}{{s}^{2}+9} \\\\ (s+4)Y(s) & =-2+\\frac{3{e}^{-\\pi s/2}}{{s}^{2}+9} \\\\ Y(s) & =-\\frac{2}{s+4}+\\frac{3{e}^{-\\pi s/2}}{({s}^{2}+9)(s+4)}\\end{aligned}\n$$",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
